4,4420,"eSOL Co.,Ltd.",IoT,設備投資・機械,,unknown,90.0,68.0,Technology,Electronics & Computer Distribution,https://www.esol.com,"eSOL Co.,Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the embedded software business in Japan. The company operates in two segments, Embedded Software Business and Sensing Solutions Business. It offers eMCOS, a scalable real-time operating system (RTOS) and hypervisor platform for software-defined computing; eMCOS SDK, a software development package; eMCOS POSIX for reliability and real-time parallelism; eMCOS Hypervisor, a real-time hypervisor for virtualization of mixed-critical applications; eT-Kernel, a microkernel-type real-time operating system based on TRON T-Kernel API; automotive open system architecture compliant in-vehicle platform software and related products. The company also provides eDEVS and eBinder for rich and modular IDE for eMCOS and eT-Kernel RTOS platforms; eMBP, a model-based parallelizer for high performance code generation on multi/manycore systems; middleware; industrial network solutions; software development kit and technical support; customer support for development and certification through engineering services; and robot operating system engineering services to automotive-related, digital home appliance, industrial equipment, digital home appliance, industrial equipment, and medical equipment manufacturers. In addition, it develops and sells hardware, such as in-vehicle printers for issuing designated slips, printers, room temperature handheld terminals, environment resistant handheld terminals, and forklift dedicated terminal holders for ham and food manufacturers, frozen food/ice cream manufacturers, wholesale and retail, warehouses and transportation, and forklifts. eSOL Co.,Ltd. was formerly known as ERG Co., Ltd. and changed its name to eSOL Co.,Ltd. in May 2001. The companywas incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Nakano, Japan.",ok,https://www.esol.com,"eSOL - Real-time embedded software platform solutions Contact us Support News Events/Seminars Blog Downloads ENGLISH ENGLISH 日本語 简体中文 Company About eSOL IR Information Technology Partners Consortium Affiliations Newsletters Careers Global Contact Products & Services Product eSOL Products Overview RTOS & Hypervisor eMCOS eMCOS SDK eMCOS POSIX eMCOS Hypervisor eT-Kernel Real-time 3D Engine eXRP New! Development Tools & Middleware eBinder/eDEVS eMBP (Model-based Parallelizer) Middleware Industrial IoT Industrial network solutions CC-Link IE TSN OPC UA AUTOSAR AUBIST Series Other Products Tailored Products Services Support & Maintenance Engineering & Professional Services ROS Engineering Services Industries/Technologies Industries Automotive Consumer Industrial Medical Technologies Multi/Many-Core Safety & Security Modern SDK Virtualization Software Frameworks AUTOSAR ROS & Autoware Case Studies News Events/Seminars Blog Downloads Contact us Support Creating the future with innovative technology. Latest news 1 / 4 Updates: eSOL Featured on the Electropages Podcast Updates: Our President, CEO and CTO, Masaki Gondo, to Speak at the ''Eclipse SDV Community Meetup'' Updates: eSOL Featured on FineEngineering Magazine Updates: eSOL Technology Forum 2026 Welcomes You in Tokyo in July! Updates: Fumiya Shigemitsu, Technology Director OS Development Engineering at eSOL, to Present on Platform Abstractions for Heterogeneous Computing at MPSoC 2026 Join our email list today for a monthly newsletter! Your browser does not support video. About eSOL eSOL is an OS vendor for the new era of cyber-physical society. We offer a platform approach that is essential to realizing software-defined systems (SDx) as well as the full-stack engineering expertise from OS to application. Learn more Strengths Strengths 1 / 4 Full Stack Engineering （FSE） SDx requires the introduction of software platforms. Updating the software OTA, for example, requires a system design taking account of all the layers of software stack, from the OS, middleware or foundation, services, and applications. It also calls for the understanding of standard APIs and cloud computing. In order to design and integrate all these software and technological layers, a full stack engineering is necessary. eSOL offers the full stack engineering from the bottom to the top, also combining the toolchain and development process into one, contributing thus to the realization of SDx. SDV （Software Defined Vehicle） SDx is an important concept for the next generation of system development and manufacturing. SDV (Software-Defined Vehicles) is a key theme in particular for the automotive industry. The SDV market is forecast to experience 20.1% annual growth through 2030 and is expected to give rise to innovative and efficient vehicles and new businesses. At eSOL, we interpret the “V” (Vehicle) in the broadest terms, encompassing not only automobiles but also railways, aircraft, robots – anything that moves. Software-first and platform approaches are indispensable for SDV development. Safety and security are also essential points to consider. eSOL boasts deep expertise and advanced technological capability cultivated through the provision of platform products and engineering services to global top-class OEMs and suppliers. With a track record as one of the few leading OS vendors in the market, we are ready to take advantage of our full-stack engineering expertise built through a broad spectrum of software development projects and contribute to the realization of SDV. Mission Critical eSOL works on a wide array of embedded systems, from automotive and industrial to medical devices, for example. Our strength lies in the development of mission-critical systems that demand high real-time availability, high performance with enhanced safety and security. As the Cyber Physical Systems (CPS) advances, including SDV, the amount of software increases further while these computers, both on the edge and in the cloud, will increasingly become mission-critical, resulting in a need for higher performance and energy efficiency. eSOL eMCOS OS offers high scalability for hundreds of processing cores. Its deterministic, real-time processing is a unique solution to the challenge of CPS. In the automotive and aerospace fields, where high performance and high safety are required, the adoption of eSOL's platform products is a testament to their reliability. Our engineering services, which we provide in conjunction with our products, have also received high praise for their technological capability and reliability. By leveraging the wealth of technical knowledge, we have gained through long years of supporting the development of these systems, we support customers in realizing ever more advanced mission-critical systems. Standardization eSOL contributes globally to industrial standardization activities in the field of automotive technologies, such as AUTOSAR, SOAFEE and the Autoware Foundation. We also contrib",pending_chatgpt_review,,,,,,
4,4420,"eSOL Co.,Ltd.",物流,物流・海運,,unknown,8.0,5.0,Technology,Electronics & Computer Distribution,https://www.esol.com,"eSOL Co.,Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the embedded software business in Japan. The company operates in two segments, Embedded Software Business and Sensing Solutions Business. It offers eMCOS, a scalable real-time operating system (RTOS) and hypervisor platform for software-defined computing; eMCOS SDK, a software development package; eMCOS POSIX for reliability and real-time parallelism; eMCOS Hypervisor, a real-time hypervisor for virtualization of mixed-critical applications; eT-Kernel, a microkernel-type real-time operating system based on TRON T-Kernel API; automotive open system architecture compliant in-vehicle platform software and related products. The company also provides eDEVS and eBinder for rich and modular IDE for eMCOS and eT-Kernel RTOS platforms; eMBP, a model-based parallelizer for high performance code generation on multi/manycore systems; middleware; industrial network solutions; software development kit and technical support; customer support for development and certification through engineering services; and robot operating system engineering services to automotive-related, digital home appliance, industrial equipment, digital home appliance, industrial equipment, and medical equipment manufacturers. In addition, it develops and sells hardware, such as in-vehicle printers for issuing designated slips, printers, room temperature handheld terminals, environment resistant handheld terminals, and forklift dedicated terminal holders for ham and food manufacturers, frozen food/ice cream manufacturers, wholesale and retail, warehouses and transportation, and forklifts. eSOL Co.,Ltd. was formerly known as ERG Co., Ltd. and changed its name to eSOL Co.,Ltd. in May 2001. The companywas incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Nakano, Japan.",ok,https://www.esol.com,"eSOL - Real-time embedded software platform solu